HTTP pattern: inspect how existing components (StudentView.vue, LecturerView.vue) make API calls -- they use native fetch with Authorization: Bearer headers. Use the same pattern (fetch, not axios). The existing notification_service.ts at the same path uses useNotifications().notify().

Base URL: /api/v1 (same origin). JWT token: localStorage.getItem('sql_quiz_token').

Export this typed error class:
  export class PracticeUnavailableError extends Error { constructor() { super('Practice unavailable while an exam is active.') } }

Export these TypeScript interfaces:
  export interface PracticeQuestion { id: number; created_by: number; target_table: string; correct_sql?: string;
    question_type: string; requirement: string; points: number; strict_ordering: boolean; strict_attrs: boolean;
    expected_result?: any; expected_columns?: any; expected_result_status: string;
    capture_error?: string; expected_result_captured_at?: string; created_at: string; updated_at: string }
  export interface PracticeAttempt { id: number; student_id: number; practice_question_id: number;
    sql_text: string; is_correct: boolean; validation_details?: any; submitted_at: string }
  export interface ValidationResult { status: string; score: number; feedback: string;
    is_correct: boolean; validation_details?: any }
  export interface PreviewResult { status: string; feedback: string; rows: Record<string, any>[];
    columns: string[]; row_count: number; truncated: boolean }

Helper: async function apiFetch(path: string, options?: RequestInit): Promise<any>
  Sets Authorization: Bearer <token> header.
  On 423 response: calls useNotifications().notify('Practice unavailable while an exam is active.', 'error');
    throws new PracticeUnavailableError().
  On other non-ok responses: reads body json, throws new Error(body.error || 'Request failed').
  On ok: returns response.json().

Student exports:
  export const listQuestions = (): Promise<PracticeQuestion[]> => apiFetch('/api/v1/practice/questions')
  export const getQuestion = (id: number): Promise<PracticeQuestion> => apiFetch(`/api/v1/practice/questions/${id}`)
  export const submit = (practiceQuestionId: number, sqlText: string): Promise<ValidationResult> =>
    apiFetch('/api/v1/practice/submit', { method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type':'application/json'},
    body: JSON.stringify({ practice_question_id: practiceQuestionId, sql_text: sqlText }) })
  export const preview = (practiceQuestionId: number, sqlText: string): Promise<PreviewResult> =>
    apiFetch('/api/v1/practice/preview', { method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type':'application/json'},
    body: JSON.stringify({ practice_question_id: practiceQuestionId, sql_text: sqlText }) })
  export const listMyAttempts = (): Promise<PracticeAttempt[]> => apiFetch('/api/v1/practice/attempts')

Lecturer exports:
  export const lecturerListQuestions = (): Promise<PracticeQuestion[]> => apiFetch('/api/v1/lecturer/practice/questions')
  export const upsertQuestion = (payload: Partial<PracticeQuestion>): Promise<any> =>
    apiFetch('/api/v1/lecturer/practice/question', { method: 'POST', ... })
  export const deleteQuestion = (id: number): Promise<void> =>
    apiFetch(`/api/v1/lecturer/practice/question/${id}`, { method: 'DELETE' })
  export const resetSandbox = (): Promise<{reset_at: string}> =>
    apiFetch('/api/v1/lecturer/practice/reset-sandbox', { method: 'POST' })
  export const lecturerPreview = (payload: {type: string; target_table: string; correct_sql: string}): Promise<any> =>
    apiFetch('/api/v1/lecturer/practice/preview', { method: 'POST', ... })

